# Element-wise arithmetic on two FIXED arrays of different static lengths is a
# COMPILE error, not a runtime abort: N is part of the type, so the compiler can
# see the mismatch. Same rule `==` already applies when it compares two fixed
# arrays element-wise -- it too requires the same static N.
#
# The exact diagnostic is locked by tests/diag/array_arith_fixlen.err; this lane
# asserts the refusal itself (nonzero exit + a non-empty diagnostic).

fn main():
    a: [3]int = [1, 2, 3]
    b: [2]int = [1, 2]
    c := a * b
    println(str(c[0]))
